        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "Data for the number of native speakers comes from ISA (2002).\r\n\r\n[mmh]: 230 (2006 FUNASA; all Mehinaku speak their mother tongue (Crevels 2007); combined Waura [wau] and Mehinaku speakers: 600 (2011); ethnic population: 230 (2006 FUNASA). Somewhat intelligible of Waurá [wau]. There is a dialect of Mehinaku called Waurá-kumá which is influenced by Waurá [wau] (2014).\r\n[wau]: 320 (Moore 2006). Ethnic population: 320 (Moore 2006). Partially intelligible of Mehináku [mmh] (2014)."
      }
    ]
